**Job Summary**

Reporting to the Director of Finance and Treasurer, the Manager of Taxation and Revenue provides strategic and operational leadership for the Town’s property taxation, assessment base management, corporate accounts receivable, and non-tax revenue functions. The Manager ensures that revenues are billed, collected, and administered accurately and on time in accordance with applicable legislation, municipal by-laws, corporate policies, and established deadlines.


The Manager maintains the integrity of tax-related systems and internal controls, and protects and maintains the assessment base. The Manager exercises the Treasurer’s delegated authority relating to taxation matters under the Municipal Act, 2001, along with other authority delegated by Council, including the approval of tax adjustment applications under sections 357 and 358.

**Job Duties Include**

The following responsibilities and duties of this position include but are not limited to:



**Leadership, Planning and Oversight**

* Communicates a consistent vision of how the Town operates, including its values and strategic plan in order to achieve the goals and objectives of the Tax and Revenue Section and Finance department;
* Accountable for the integrity and administration of the Town’s taxation and revenue functions, compliance with statutory and corporate requirements, effective collection of amounts owing to the Town, protection of the municipal assessment base, and stewardship and control of tax and non-tax revenues.
* Provides options and recommendations to Director of Finance and Senior Management Committee for achieving department, section and corporate objectives;
* Develops and monitors annual work plans with a thorough understanding of required outputs and timelines, and oversees special projects, such as software upgrades;
* Acts as a corporate resource for interdepartmental special projects and corporate committees. Leads and completes special projects and studies requiring extensive research and analysis and develops recommendations based on findings.
* Participates in annual budget planning in line with department and corporate needs, and conducts the analysis needed to inform the Tax and Revenue Section’s requirements;
* Motivates, coaches and guides staff. Ensures individual training and development plans are in place to develop capability to meet current and future requirements. Ensures that cross training supports seamless service to all clients;
Supports an environment of continuous improvement and innovation.  



**Property Taxation Administration and Compliance**

* Ensures the integrity and accuracy of the taxation billing system to ensure all taxes for the Region, School Boards and Town are collected and managed in accordance with the Municipal Act, Region tax by-laws, and provincial legislation;
* Balances tax rolls for accurate and timely interim, final and supplementary billing. This includes calculating tax rates and maintaining tax information within the Online Property Tax Analysis (OPTA) database to meet tax billing deadlines;
* Oversees the Assessment Base Management (ABM) program, including policies, procedures and processes to protect and enhance the Town’s assessment base;
* Participates in Assessment Review Board hearings for properties with broader impacts on assessment base;
* Maintains current knowledge of legislation and judicial decisions affecting taxation, and analyzes their impact to identify and implement changes that ensure compliance;
* Responsible for all tax sale registration accounts, ensuring accuracy, compliance with statutory deadlines and timely resolution;
* Prepares and presents reports to General Government Committee and Council including Tax Rate By-laws and tax status reports;
Balances and completes the annual external taxation financial reporting (Financial Information Return) annually;  



**Customer Relations**

* Responds to complex complaints and requests for information including detailed explanations of assessment, rebate programs and collections;

Communicates with, develops and monitors internal and external relationships to ensure timely and accurate resolution of complex assessment or other issues;  



**Accounts Receivable and Non-Tax Revenue**

* Oversees corporate accounts receivable and non-tax billing, ensuring invoices are accurate, appropriately authorized, and processed in a timely manner;
* Responsible for receivables administration and collection activities, including ageing reports, outstanding accounts, collection follow-up and effective customer account management;
* Oversees payment and cashiering functions, ensuring accurate and timely processing and appropriate controls are maintained;
Establishes consistent standards and procedures for customer account creation and maintenance, invoicing, account enquiries, collections and revenue administration across Town departments.  



**Qualifications/Skills**

* Three (3) year College diploma in Business Administration or a related field, or an approved equivalent combination of education and relevant Municipal experience;
* Formal technical/professional certification through Municipal Tax Administration Program (MTAP) or Municipal Revenue Administration Program (MRAP), and holds the Certified Municipal Revenue Professional (CMRP) designation;
* Minimum 9 years progressively responsible experience in taxation, with a minimum 5 year supervisory experience or a combination of training, education and experience deemed equivalent;
* Experience in development and implementation of effective tax strategies, including policies, procedures, processes, systems, and internal control;
* Thorough understanding and able to interpret, understand and apply various tax legislations and rules and requirements under the Municipal Act;
* Background in providing professional advice, assistance and direction to staff and Council;
Practical experience in the full cycle of tax billing and collection of taxes.  



**Nice to Have**

* Chartered Professional Accountant (CPA) designation is considered an asset;
* Completion of AMCTO Municipal Administration Program (MAP) and Certified Municipal Officer (CMO) designation would be an asset;
Management experience in a unionized environment is an asset.  

**What is Offered to Staff**

* **Compensation:** We offer competitive pay that reflects the responsibilities of the position.
* **Hours of Work:** This is a non-union full-time position that works 35 hours per week. The hours of work are Monday to Friday from 8:30 a.m. - 4:30 p.m.
* **Benefits** : The Town offers full-time staff a comprehensive benefit package with paid sick, vacation and personal leave days; Parental Leave Top-up; Employee & Family Assistance Program; Health & Wellness Program, Town of Ajax Fitness Centre membership; plus a defined benefits pension (OMERS pension - https://www.omers.com/ ).
* **Hybrid Work Program** : The Town offers a Hybrid Work Program. A flexible work arrangement is currently a possibility with this position, and can be discussed during the interview process.

**How to Apply**

If this opportunity matches your interest and experience, please click the “Apply” button and apply by 11:59 p.m. on the closing date:

December 6, 2026

**Vacancy Statement**

All job postings issued by the Town of Ajax are intended to fill existing vacant positions unless otherwise stated.

**Are you a current Town of Ajax employee?**

If you are a current Town of Ajax, please apply internally through the **Jobs Hub** app of your Workday account in order for your application to be processed as an internal applicant.

