**POSITION**  
As the facility manager, the incumbent will oversee operational management of VIA Rail’s real estate activities in 3rd party shared stations as well as for VIA Rail’s own portfolio of railway stations. This includes major terminals as well as smaller stations, shelters and train platforms.



Key responsibilities for this position include overseeing the operational execution of preventive maintenance program, asset management program, operational project and suppliers performance management.



The facility manager will also participate in the strategic plans and initiatives development for is portfolio of properties aligned with VIA Rail’s asset management policies & programs, regulatory requirements as well as stakeholder, corporate and departmental vision / mandate in delivering safe, efficient, sustainable and customer focused facilities for its users.



**RESPONSIBILITIES :**

* Operate and coordinate the different action in the station in accordance with the defined action plan and strategies;
* Participate in the development of strategic initiatives and activities to improve maintenance program efficiency and cost effectiveness;
* Conduct supplier performance evaluation and make sure to address any problematic with the key stakeholders;
* Represent the Real Estate group as a liaison officer with internal client (Customer Experience, Train Operation etc.) as well as with external tenant and concession operators;
* He is a reference point of contact for our Facility Service desk;
* Act as the field representative to raise, coordinated and supervise the realization of operational project;
* Accountable to deliver on time and on budget the expected project for his region;
* Participate in the development of the property profiles containing the strategic and operational action plans and recommendations for each property;
* Responsible to coordinate (perform by himself or by subcontractor) site inspections and documenting the various data used to populate and update the property profile;
* Responsible to monitor the evolution of the budget allocation and ensure that they are aligned with the business needs and priorities;
* Approve the expense and act as the point of contact for Facility Call Center;
* Ensure that the operations are cost effective and optimized to the benefits of VIA passengers, visitors and employees that are using our stations.


**WHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR :**



* University degree in business or property management in combination with another related designation in property management or real estate;
* Minimum of 5 years of relative experience in real estate and property management with a clear broad knowledge and understanding of the complexities of real estate industry and asset management with diverse stakeholders;
* Excellent leadership, managerial and strategic planning skills;
* Must be rigorous, results oriented and flexible;
* Able to work in a complex, changing environment with multiple tasks;
* Excellent analytical and problem-solving skills;
* Self-motivated with the ability to work under pressure with tight deadlines;
* Strong oral & written communication skills in both English (mandatory) and in French (preferred) and effective business acumen;
* Professionalism, flexibility and ability to work both in a team-oriented environment and independently;
* Ability to interpret site and building drawings, with full understanding of real estate terminology;
* Technical knowledge and skills (SharePoint databases, Excel, Word, PowerPoint);
* Demonstrated commitment to operate for a service-oriented company;
* Demonstrated knowledge of market trends, market rents, market conditions, understanding principles of market value.


